<title>NORWAY: Norway August CPI falls 0.1 pct month/month.</title>
<headline>Norway August CPI falls 0.1 pct month/month.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics Norway issued the following economic indicator.</p>
<p> NORWAY CONSUMER PRICES    AUG 1996  JULY 1996    AUG 1995</p>
<p>(in percent)</p>
<p>  Month-on-month change     -0.1	+0.4	   -0.2</p>
<p>  Year-on-year change	 +1.5	+1.3	   +2.2</p>
<p>  Index (base 1979)	  263.7     263.9	  259.9</p>
<p>NOTE -- Eight economists polled by Reuters forecast month-on-month inflation to be roughly unchanged in August. The range for the monthly CPI was between -0.2 and +0.1 percent.</p>
<p>Statistics Norway attributed the 0.1 percent month-on-month fall to a seasonal drop in the prices of clothes, shoes and vegetables.   --Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
